# Roger all

When the user says **"roger all"** (any casing), run the full maintenance pass — do not skip steps.

**Roger all is not a git commit.** It means run audits, fix blocking failures, and align docs/rules — commit only when the user explicitly asks.

## Command

```bash
npm run roger:all
```

Optional flags:

```bash
npm run roger:all -- --fix       # ESLint auto-fix, then full gate
npm run roger:all -- --relaxed   # Skip strict blocking on code/CSS/i18n warnings
```

`npm run audit` and `npm run roger:all` use **strict mode by default**. Use `npm run audit:relaxed` or `npm run roger:relaxed` for the old advisory-only gate.

## What roger:all runs

1. `npm run lint:fix` — only with `--fix`
2. `npm run sync:i18n` — key parity from `en.js`
3. `npm run audit:docs-sync` — `09-implementation-status.md` vs code
4. `npm run audit` — full gate (deps, CSS, UI, i18n, code, tests, types, build, governance, sync)

## After the script

Fix every **blocking FAIL** until `npm run roger:all` exits 0. Then:

- Update docs/rules if product direction changed (mobile-only, no PWA install, localhost phone shell)
- Update `docs/CHANGELOG.md` for user-visible changes
- Do **not** commit unless the user asks

## Product defaults (keep docs/code aligned)

- **Distribution:** Android APK (Capacitor dev) + Play Store TWA + iOS Capacitor — not a consumer web/PWA product
- **Localhost dev:** full-screen phone shell via `src/ui/dev/DevPhoneFrame.jsx` — always on, no exit toggle
- **UI shell:** bottom nav only — no desktop top nav
- **Loading:** single `PageLoader` (P logo + Starting Perovo) for boot and route Suspense
- **Cloud:** local-first; manual restore only (`cloud-sync-local-first` rule)
- **i18n:** `t("key")` only in UI; run sync after new `en.js` keys

